IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `voc-dates`
IMPORT `voc-rules`

-- Victims of Crime (Financial Assistance Scheme) Act 2022 (Vic) -- the questions of the VICTIM who applies for
-- financial assistance.
--
-- SEAT: the individual who applies for financial assistance from the scheme decision maker: a primary victim (injured by,
-- or trying to stop, an act of violence), a secondary victim (who witnessed it, or the parent of a child victim), a related
-- victim (family, dependant or partner of a person killed), or the person who paid for that person's funeral. "Am I a
-- victim under the scheme?", "How much can I be paid?", "By when must I apply?", "Must my application be refused?", "Can I
-- have the decision reviewed, and by when?", "How much can I be made to repay?". The scheme decision maker, VCAT, the
-- police and the offender get no seat: the decision maker's satisfactions, opinions and determinations are asked as facts.
--
-- Every question takes plain facts (yes/no, numbers, dates, a choice from a list) and calls the rules of voc-rules.l4. The
-- rules with deadlines (ss 23, 27, 45, 46) are DEONTIC rules run inside; no question takes a DEONTIC or an EVENT.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: quotations from a plain-text conversion by Legalese Commons of the Word file of the Victims of Crime
-- (Financial Assistance Scheme) Act 2022, Version No. 002 (1 December 2025), not the authorised version. (c) State of
-- Victoria; published with the authority of the Government Printer for the State of Victoria. No part may be reproduced
-- except in accordance with the Copyright Act 1968 (Cth). Quoted under the owner's ruling of 24 October 2026
